                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-9">See &ldquo;Policy Normalization Principles and Plans,&rdquo; FOMC, September 17, 2014 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/press/monetary/20140917c.htm">https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/press/monetary/20140917c.htm</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-9" aria-label="Return from footnote 9.">Return to 9</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-10">See &ldquo;FOMC Issues Addendum to the Policy Normalization Principles and Plans,&rdquo; Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System press release, June 14, 2017 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20170614c.htm">https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20170614c.htm</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-10" aria-label="Return from footnote 10.">Return to 10</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-11">See the FOMC post-meeting statement of July 26, 2017 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20170726a.htm">https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20170726a.htm</a>).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-11" aria-label="Return from footnote 11.">Return to 11</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-12">Once started, the plan is to allow up to $6 billion a month of maturing Treasuries and $4 billion a month of principal payments of agency MBS and agency debt to run off the balance sheet. These caps would be increased by $6 billion and $4 billion per month, respectively, every three months, until they reach $30 billion per month for Treasuries and $20 billion per month for agency MBS and agency debt. Thereafter, those caps would be maintained and the balance sheet would gradually decline. (See &ldquo;FOMC Issues Addendum to the Policy Normalization Principles and Plans,&rdquo; Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System press release, June 14, 2017 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20170614c.htm">https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20170614c.htm</a>) ).<br />
For projections of the Fed&rsquo;s balance sheet under various scenarios, see &ldquo;Projections for the SOMA Portfolio and Net Income,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of New York, July 2017 (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/markets/omo/SOMAPortfolioandIncomeProjections_July2017Update.pdf">https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/markets/omo/SOMAPortfolioandIncomeProjections_July2017Update.pdf</a>).
